00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.713
They used to tell me when I was three

00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:32.562
I would grab people at weddings and just

00:00:32.562 --> 00:00:34.390
dance with them out of nowhere.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.322
- He did that last week, too.

00:00:37.698 --> 00:00:39.878
- Oooo, we all said oldest.

00:00:40.116 --> 00:00:42.438
- Taking that party title.

00:00:42.696 --> 00:00:44.340
- I'm not saying I'm the life of the party

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.292
in all situations.

00:00:46.292 --> 00:00:48.364
- Well, you do love a good party.

00:00:48.364 --> 00:00:49.407
- I do love parties.

00:00:49.502 --> 00:00:51.896
- [Voiceover] So, it's
actually middle children.

00:00:51.896 --> 00:00:52.749
(buzzing)

00:00:52.749 --> 00:00:53.954
No one guessed right.

00:00:54.597 --> 00:00:55.985
- Oh, okay.

00:00:56.121 --> 00:00:57.015
- I think so.

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:57.990
- Only Megan.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.990
- A study found which sibling
tends to be a perfectionist.

00:01:03.387 --> 00:01:05.094
- I don't think we even
have to discuss this one.

00:01:05.094 --> 00:01:06.008
- No.
- We just all know.

00:01:06.008 --> 00:01:07.207
- Want to say it all together?

00:01:07.207 --> 00:01:08.710
- One, two, three.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:09.808
Middle child.
- Middle child.

00:01:09.808 --> 00:01:14.101
If the science is science,
it would trend this way.

00:01:14.379 --> 00:01:16.065
- Oooo, we said the -

00:01:16.065 --> 00:01:20.637
- Since when?

00:01:20.637 --> 00:01:21.815
It's you.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:25.188
For instance, you were cooking those like

00:01:25.188 --> 00:01:27.951
egg wraps from that cookbook.

00:01:27.951 --> 00:01:29.209
She didn't get it right the first time.

00:01:29.209 --> 00:01:30.917
She made it the next day.

00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:33.294
You have plans to make it again.

00:01:33.294 --> 00:01:35.427
- [Voiceover] Yep,
Emily, you guessed right.

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:37.378
(bell rings) It is oldest children.

00:01:37.378 --> 00:01:38.841
- Oh, you were right.

00:01:38.841 --> 00:01:40.588
- I knew it.

00:01:40.588 --> 00:01:44.265
- Maybe I'm just trying
to not be a perfectionist.

00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:46.194
- Which sibling has been shown to be

00:01:46.194 --> 00:01:48.674
most empathetic of the family?

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:51.070
- Oldest, for sure.
- How it is.

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:52.543
I think he's the most emphathetic.

00:01:52.543 --> 00:01:53.730
- I was basing it on my -

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:54.664
- He knows it.

00:01:54.664 --> 00:01:55.314
- It's true.

00:01:56.018 --> 00:01:57.243
- Oh.
- Oh.

00:01:57.441 --> 00:01:59.472
- I definitely think
that Jessica's the most

00:01:59.472 --> 00:02:01.484
empathetic of all of us,

00:02:01.484 --> 00:02:03.942
because you're very sweet and kind.

00:02:03.942 --> 00:02:05.852
- You always send a followup text.

00:02:05.852 --> 00:02:08.371
- I use those emoji things on the text.

00:02:08.371 --> 00:02:09.529
- Oh, yeah, the emojis?

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:10.240
- I like those.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:10.911
- Exactly.

00:02:10.911 --> 00:02:12.394
- [Voiceover] Yes, that's right.

00:02:12.394 --> 00:02:13.958
Younger children have been shown

00:02:13.958 --> 00:02:15.894
to be the most empathetic. (bell rings)

00:02:16.965 --> 00:02:18.678
- Yay!
- Yay!

